== 6.3 Digital Connectivity & National Optical Fibre Infrastructure
The advent of digital telecommunications and internet technologies has revolutionized India's socio-economic landscape. The convergence of mobile tele-density, low-cost broadband data, and the Aadhaar-based digital identity stack has positioned India as one of the world's largest digital societies.

The *BharatNet Project* (originally launched as the National Optical Fibre Network - NOFN in October 2011) seeks to establish a high-speed broadband network backbone connecting over 250,000 Gram Panchayats across the nation. This fiber-optic infrastructure delivers digital delivery of governance (e-panchayat), telemedicine, online education, and direct benefit transfer (DBT) payments to rural citizens.

